    "description": "Single source of truth for artifact/task -> skill routing. scripts/route.sh reads this; the table in skills/forensics-router/SKILL.md must agree (scripts/test-routing.sh checks).",
    "fallbackId": "R0",
    "scoring": "For every keyword rule whose `mustAll` all match and `exclude` does not, the route scores `weight` (default 1) per DISTINCT string matched by `must`. Rules that identify the ARTIFACT TYPE (extension, `file -b` signature, well-known artifact filename) carry weight 2 so they beat topic words. Highest score wins; ties broken by position in `priority`; no match -> fallbackId. Matching is case-insensitive over: request text + `file -b` output + filename(s).",
    "notes": [
      "Routes are about the ARTIFACT you were handed, not about the question. A question about 'when was X run' on a disk image is disk-image first, then windows-artifacts.",
      "Several skills often apply to one case (disk-image -> windows-artifacts -> anti-forensics-timeline). PRIMARY is where you start; SECONDARY candidates are listed by route.sh."
    ]
  },
